Based on the provided legal context, let's analyze the conditions for naturalization in Vietnam specified in Clause 1, Article 19 of the Law on Vietnamese Nationality 2008.

The conditions are as follows:

a) Have full civil act capacity as prescribed by Vietnamese law;
b) Comply with the Constitution and law of Vietnam; respect traditions, customs and practices of Vietnamese people;
c) Know Vietnamese enough to integrate into Vietnamese community;
d) Have resided in Vietnam for at least 5 years by the time of applying for naturalized Vietnamese nationality;
dd) Have ability to ensure life in Vietnam.

The question asks whether an Australian can be naturalized into Vietnamese nationality after 3 years of living in Vietnam. Let's examine the conditions:

* Condition d) requires the applicant to have resided in Vietnam for at least 5 years by the time of applying for naturalized Vietnamese nationality. Since the applicant has only lived in Vietnam for 3 years, they do not meet this condition.

Therefore, based on the provided legal context, an Australian cannot be naturalized into Vietnamese nationality after 3 years of living in Vietnam because they do not meet the condition of having resided in Vietnam for at least 5 years.

